<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  PodCarIsLandspeeder.xml                   Jawa_Patches - new file 2026-08-24
  ============================================================================

  Reskins Core's `AncientPodCar` as a wrecked landspeeder. Owner's request,
  2026-08-24: "reskin the Ancient Podcar graphic and name to be Wrecked
  Landspeeder ... pretty ancient and destroyed, already mostly looted and sun
  scorched."

  APPEARANCE ONLY. `size`, `fillPercent`, `passability`, `pathCost`,
  `MaxHitPoints` and `killedLeavings` are all left as Core wrote them, so every
  ancient-ruin PrefabDef and MapGenerator that places one keeps placing one and
  it behaves identically. Three strings and one texPath change, nothing else.

  WHY A NEW texPath RATHER THAN AN OVERRIDING LOOSE PNG. Core's art lives in
  `resources.assets`, and a loose mod PNG at the same path would win regardless
  of load order - which works, but leaves no way to tell from the def whether
  the swap happened. Repointing texPath makes the reskin visible in the def
  dump and reversible by deleting one Replace.

  ⚠️ `rotatable` is false and `graphicClass` is `Graphic_Single`, so this is
  ONE view and there is no `_north`/`_east` sibling to keep in step.

  ⚠️ The texture is 512x256 (2:1) against a `drawSize` of (3,2) (1.5:1), which
  is the same shape mismatch Core's own PodCar.png (256x128) carries - the
  engine compresses the art into the quad, and the art is drawn pre-stretched to
  survive it. Do not "fix" the canvas to 3:2; that would squash the hull.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="AncientPodCar"]/label</xpath>
    <value>
      <label>wrecked landspeeder</label>
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="AncientPodCar"]/description</xpath>
    <value>
      <description>A civilian repulsorlift speeder, dead on the sand for longer than anyone here can count. The canopy is gone, the drive coils were pulled out of it generations ago, and what the salvagers left the sun has been bleaching and cooking ever since. Sand has drifted into the cockpit well and packed itself solid.</description>
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="AncientPodCar"]/graphicData/texPath</xpath>
    <value>
      <texPath>Things/Building/Ruins/WreckedLandspeeder</texPath>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
